ia but  really also learning these more softer  professional skills that of course are  so important to present well to  communicate well do this in front of  very senior audiences do this in front  of board members this is exactly what  you will learn in the mba where also i  personally took so much away at my ncr  experience so here with me i have  federica from the mba class of zhang  garden of 2022 thank you for joining me  federica thank you for inviting me can  you share a little bit about your  background what did you do prior to the  mba yes of course i'm italian  i've studied  mathematics in italy and then had a bit  of experience in project management  mainly in the fashion industry  so what is the course here in zhang that  so far you enjoyed most what was the  most significant learning for you i have  to say that i really enjoyed capital  markets  course this is something i really never  did before  but a teaching method was so  diverse and also we had the impression  to really learn  something that is happening in the world  and very important for every mba student  that very much resonates because this is  also my experience when i did my mba or  maybe for the uninitiated out there can  you share a couple of thoughts on like  what's distinctive about the mba  teaching method how does it work here in  zangai what makes it special of course  so i've studied in italy university and  the methodology was completely different  like a professor telling you things  things same things you have to study a  lot and then finally have an exam here  the story is completely different you  always have group works to do different  methods like  of course frontal lessons but also  discussions  uh workshops and a lot of exams also  exactly i mean that's really i think the  point of an mba it's not so much about  academia but it's really about hands-on  management and business knowledge and  this of course is what makes it valuable  do you happen to look back at the last  weeks already one key memorable moment  that you want to share  so  first of all i have to say that the  first day of mba was memorable because  it was the first time being together  with almost 50 people in the same big  room and you know after this covet  period this was so strange to be all  together uh  really shaking hands and meeting people  that were all really happy to start this  journey together this was the super  the the most exciting moment i have to  say so that's amazing thank you  appreciate it  so it's a pleasure to also meet you  alisa you're also part of the current  mba cohort so i'm standing here with  payet who's also part of the current mba  class thank you mcloy for taking your  time as well part of the current mba  cohort at zangalan thank you for joining  me mate much appreciated thank you ali  for joining me here as well at the  university of zangalan so before the mba  i was a finance professional i've got  around five years of experience with the  fmcg industry but i've lived in the last  six years in finland and i was working  in operational procurement for and  manufacturing company uh so i worked in  financial industries i was a regional  manager in insurance company  last year before joining the mba i spent  a year in digital transformation of the  same 120 year old insurance company  and i also co-founded to two companies  i was working in ministry of treasury  and finance for for the last nine years  the last three years i worked as a  project manager and government consulter  i  am a phd in music theory  i was a concert pianist before that i've  been working as a sustainability  consultant so far what i really like  here is that we get to meet all these  different companies because that's  something that you don't really get to  do at school or in your normal work so  of course like  being exposed to so many companies is  something that i really appreciate for  example on the turkey day i went to a  company called on running and 